      "source": [
        "# Problem: Dropout Regularization in Feedforward Neural Networks\n",
        "\n",
        "## Problem Statement\n",
        "You are tasked with investigating the effect of **dropout regularization** on the generalization performance of feedforward neural networks. Using the **MNIST** dataset, you will:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Implement a feedforward neural network for digit classification\n",
        "2. Train multiple models with different dropout rates (0.0, 0.2, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7)\n",
        "3. Compare training and validation loss curves to identify overfitting\n",
        "4. Determine the optimal dropout rate for best generalization\n",
        "\n",
        "### Learning Objectives\n",
        "- Understand how dropout prevents overfitting\n",
        "- Analyze the tradeoff between model capacity and regularization\n",
        "- Interpret training dynamics through loss curves\n",
        "- Select hyperparameters based on validation performance\n",
        "\n",
        "### Requirements\n",
        "1. **Data Acquisition**: Load and preprocess the MNIST dataset\n",
        "2. **Data Wrangling**: Normalize pixel values and create train/validation splits\n",
        "3. **Model Implementation**: Build a feedforward network with configurable dropout\n",
        "4. **Training**: Train models with various dropout rates using cross-entropy loss\n",
        "5. **Evaluation**: Plot loss curves and compare test accuracies\n",
        "\n",
        "<details>\n",
        "  <summary>💡 Hint</summary>\n",
        "  Use `nn.Dropout()` layers between fully connected layers. Remember that dropout behaves differently during training vs evaluation (use `model.train()` and `model.eval()`). Track both training and validation losses at each epoch for plotting.\n",
        "</details>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 1: Data Acquisition\n",
        "\n",
        "Load the **MNIST** dataset using `torchvision.datasets`. This dataset contains 70,000 grayscale images of handwritten digits (0-9), each 28×28 pixels."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 1,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import torch\n",
        "import torch.nn as nn\n",
        "import torch.optim as optim\n",
        "import torchvision\n",
        "import torchvision.transforms as transforms\n",
        "from torch.utils.data import DataLoader, random_split\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 2,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Downloading http://yann.lecun.com/exdb/mnist/train-images-idx3-ubyte.gz\n",
            "Downloading http://yann.lecun.com/exdb/mnist/train-labels-idx1-ubyte.gz\n",
            "Downloading http://yann.lecun.com/exdb/mnist/t10k-images-idx3-ubyte.gz\n",
            "Downloading http://yann.lecun.com/exdb/mnist/t10k-labels-idx1-ubyte.gz\n",
            "Processing...\n",
            "Done!\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Load MNIST dataset\n",
        "transform = transforms.Compose([\n",
        "    transforms.ToTensor(),\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "train_dataset = torchvision.datasets.MNIST(root='./data', train=True, download=True, transform=transform)\n",
        "test_dataset = torchvision.datasets.MNIST(root='./data', train=False, download=True, transform=transform)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Training samples: {len(train_dataset)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Test samples: {len(test_dataset)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 2: Data Wrangling\n",
        "\n",
        "Preprocess the data:\n",
        "- Normalize pixel values to [0, 1] range (done automatically by ToTensor)\n",
        "- Split training data into train and validation sets (80/20 split)\n",
        "- Create DataLoaders with appropriate batch size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 3,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Training samples: 48000\n",
            "Validation samples: 12000\n",
            "Test samples: 10000\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Split training dataset into train and validation (80/20)\n",
        "train_size = int(0.8 * len(train_dataset))\n",
        "val_size = len(train_dataset) - train_size\n",
        "train_subset, val_subset = random_split(train_dataset, [train_size, val_size])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create DataLoaders\n",
        "batch_size = 64\n",
        "train_loader = DataLoader(train_subset, batch_size=batch_size, shuffle=True)\n",
        "val_loader = DataLoader(val_subset, batch_size=batch_size, shuffle=False)\n",
        "test_loader = DataLoader(test_dataset, batch_size=batch_size, shuffle=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Training samples: {len(train_subset)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Validation samples: {len(val_subset)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Test samples: {len(test_dataset)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 3: Model Implementation\n",
        "\n",
        "Implement a feedforward neural network with:\n",
        "- Input layer: 784 units (28×28 flattened)\n",
        "- Hidden layers: 2 layers with 256 units each\n",
        "- Dropout layers: Applied after each hidden layer (configurable rate)\n",
        "- Output layer: 10 units (one per digit class)\n",
        "- Activation: ReLU for hidden layers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 4,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class FeedforwardNN(nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, dropout_rate=0.0):\n",
        "        super(FeedforwardNN, self).__init__()\n",
        "        self.fc1 = nn.Linear(28 * 28, 256)\n",
        "        self.dropout1 = nn.Dropout(dropout_rate)\n",
        "        self.fc2 = nn.Linear(256, 256)\n",
        "        self.dropout2 = nn.Dropout(dropout_rate)\n",
        "        self.fc3 = nn.Linear(256, 10)\n",
        "        self.relu = nn.ReLU()\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def forward(self, x):\n",
        "        x = x.view(x.size(0), -1)  # Flatten\n",
        "        x = self.relu(self.fc1(x))\n",
        "        x = self.dropout1(x)\n",
        "        x = self.relu(self.fc2(x))\n",
        "        x = self.dropout2(x)\n",
        "        x = self.fc3(x)\n",
        "        return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 4: Training\n",
        "\n",
        "Train models with different dropout rates:\n",
        "- Dropout rates: [0.0, 0.2, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7]\n",
        "- Loss function: CrossEntropyLoss\n",
        "- Optimizer: Adam with learning rate 0.001\n",
        "- Epochs: 20\n",
        "- Track training and validation loss at each epoch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 5,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def train_model(model, train_loader, val_loader, epochs=20, lr=0.001):\n",
        "    criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n",
        "    optimizer = optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=lr)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    train_losses = []\n",
        "    val_losses = []\n",
        "    \n",
        "    for epoch in range(epochs):\n",
        "        # Training phase\n",
        "        model.train()\n",
        "        train_loss = 0.0\n",
        "        for images, labels in train_loader:\n",
        "            optimizer.zero_grad()\n",
        "            outputs = model(images)\n",
        "            loss = criterion(outputs, labels)\n",
        "            loss.backward()\n",
        "            optimizer.step()\n",
        "            train_loss += loss.item()\n",
        "        \n",
        "        train_loss /= len(train_loader)\n",
        "        train_losses.append(train_loss)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Validation phase\n",
        "        model.eval()\n",
        "        val_loss = 0.0\n",
        "        with torch.no_grad():\n",
        "            for images, labels in val_loader:\n",
        "                outputs = model(images)\n",
        "                loss = criterion(outputs, labels)\n",
        "                val_loss += loss.item()\n",
        "        \n",
        "        val_loss /= len(val_loader)\n",
        "        val_losses.append(val_loss)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        if (epoch + 1) % 5 == 0:\n",
        "            print(f\"Epoch [{epoch + 1}/{epochs}], Train Loss: {train_loss:.4f}, Val Loss: {val_loss:.4f}\")\n",
        "    \n",
        "    return train_losses, val_losses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 6,
      "metadata": {},
